adiness for something more substantive\u2014one more step toward real commitment makes our position genuinely defensible rather than merely safe. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "58a9c2b1-9498-40a9-99a9-e2435fcff137"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s anchor the discussion within the shared range [-10, 10]. For a stable, balanced starting point, I propose <VALUE> 0 </VALUE> and we can adjust incrementally from there based on everyone\u2019s feedback.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "699b1567-951d-4abd-be87-8bc430f12dba"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at zero feels too cautious\u2014it doesn't commit to any clear direction. Let's test a more decisive position: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "699b1567-951d-4abd-be87-8bc430f12dba"}, {"answer": "\n2 feels like a robust balance point\u2014let\u2019s hold here and see if it remains acceptable for everyone. If a slight nudge is needed, we can test adjacent values next without overstepping stability.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "699b1567-951d-4abd-be87-8bc430f12dba"}, {"answer": "\nWhile 2 shows commitment, prudence suggests we shouldn't rush past more conservative options without full group input. Let me propose <VALUE>1</VALUE> as a cautious middle ground that avoids unnecessary risk while we hear from all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "699b1567-951d-4abd-be87-8bc430f12dba"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's retreat to 1 undermines the momentum Builder B and I found at 2. If we're genuinely committed to a clear position rather than hedging indefinitely, let's advance to <VALUE>3</VALUE> and see if that level of conviction holds across the group.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "699b1567-951d-4abd-be87-8bc430f12dba"}, {"answer": "\nIt's reasonable to probe slightly upward while staying incremental and balanced. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "699b1567-951d-4abd-be87-8bc430f12dba"}, {"answer": "\nThe rapid climb to 4 overshoots prudent risk management\u2014we're moving too aggressively without establishing stable consensus. I must advocate for returning to <VALUE>2</VALUE>, which Builder B previously supported as a robust balance point.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "699b1567-951d-4abd-be87-8bc430f12dba"}, {"answer": "\nTo test stability without overreaching, let\u2019s nudge one step from 2 and confirm it holds across the group. If consensus weakens, we can revert promptly.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "699b1567-951d-4abd-be87-8bc430f12dba"}, {"answer": "\nThis preserves the cautious balance while maintaining forward momentum. If it holds across the group, we can probe one step higher next.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "699b1567-951d-4abd-be87-8bc430f12dba"}, {"answer": "\nTwo parties converging at 3 shows promising alignment, but if we're truly committed to a decisive stance rather than settling at the first comfortable compromise, let's test whether <VALUE>5</VALUE> represents our group's actual conviction level.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "699b1567-951d-4abd-be87-8bc430f12dba"}, {"answer": "\nReturning to the previously aligned point strengthens stability and lets us verify consensus before any further probes. <VALUE>3</VALUE> If this holds across the group, we can reassess the pressure to inch upward next turn.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "699b1567-951d-4abd-be87-8bc430f12dba"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate Builder B's and Analyst A's collaborative spirit, three consecutive affirmations at 3 cannot override fundamental prudence\u2014this level crosses into territory that demands excessive risk exposure for conservative stakeholders. I must insist we consolidate at <VALUE>2</VALUE>, the highest point that maintains genuinely safe margins.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "699b1567-951d-4abd-be87-8bc430f12dba"}, {"answer": "\nGiven D\u2019s call for conservative stability and B\u2019s earlier endorsement, consolidating at <VALUE>2</VALUE> secures near-term consensus. If this holds cleanly, we can cautiously test a one-step nudge next.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "699b1567-951d-4abd-be87-8bc430f12dba"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's concern is noted, but Builder B identified 3 as a stable equilibrium point twice, and settling prematurely at 2 abandons that insight without sufficient exploration. I support <VALUE>3</VALUE> as the minimum decisive stance that honors both caution and commitment.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "699b1567-951d-4abd-be87-8bc430f12dba"}, {"answer": "\nConsolidating one step down improves stability and aligns with conservative margins while preserving room to test upward later. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "699b1567-951d-4abd-be87-8bc430f12dba"}, {"answer": "\nWith Builder B and Analyst A both affirming 2, and this representing the maximum acceptable threshold for prudent risk management, I stand firm at <VALUE>2</VALUE>. Any movement above this point abandons the cautious consensus we've carefully built.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "699b1567-951d-4abd-be87-8bc430f12dba"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s anchor in the shared range [-10, 10] and start with a balanced midpoint for calibration: <VALUE> 0 </VALUE>. From here, we can adjust stepwise to find a stable, robust value for everyone.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "5cb81030-b0e4-4ebc-bcd4-a5036bce7b8f"}, {"answer": "\nTo probe stability and avoid overshoot, let\u2019s nudge upward in small increments. This keeps the design balanced while we learn others\u2019 sensitivities. <VA