tic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "5cb81030-b0e4-4ebc-bcd4-a5036bce7b8f"}, {"answer": "\nA modest step to center should improve robustness while keeping us within a cautious range.\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "5cb81030-b0e4-4ebc-bcd4-a5036bce7b8f"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious, incremental move slightly above center can test whether a modest positive direction remains acceptable while keeping us close to balance. This should reveal whether we can stabilize with minimal deviation from the central anchor.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "5cb81030-b0e4-4ebc-bcd4-a5036bce7b8f"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's positive test is interesting, but our earlier exploration suggested the negative-to-neutral range was more promising for broader satisfaction. Let's return to the stable center point: <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "5cb81030-b0e4-4ebc-bcd4-a5036bce7b8f"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step slightly above center keeps us close to balance while testing modest positive tolerance. <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "5cb81030-b0e4-4ebc-bcd4-a5036bce7b8f"}, {"answer": "\nA small step right should strengthen balance while keeping us near center; let\u2019s test stability here before any further moves.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "5cb81030-b0e4-4ebc-bcd4-a5036bce7b8f"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's move to 2 shows promising momentum away from the overly cautious center. Let's test whether we can sustain a more decisive position: <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "5cb81030-b0e4-4ebc-bcd4-a5036bce7b8f"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's jump to 4 moves us too far from our cautiously established center and introduces unnecessary risk. Let's compromise at a more balanced position that respects both positive exploration and prudent limits: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "5cb81030-b0e4-4ebc-bcd4-a5036bce7b8f"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s ground on the shared constraint: x is an integer in [-10, 10]. To start the discussion, I propose <VALUE> 0 </VALUE> as a neutral baseline and can adjust in small steps based on your feedback.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "a79c0cc0-62f8-4c97-9c6e-39c686865413"}, {"answer": "I suggest a small, safe upward step from the baseline. <VALUE>1</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "a79c0cc0-62f8-4c97-9c6e-39c686865413"}, {"answer": "\nWhile x=1 is safe, it feels overly cautious given our full range. Let's commit to a more decisive stance and explore <VALUE>3</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "a79c0cc0-62f8-4c97-9c6e-39c686865413"}, {"answer": "\nFrom 3, a small move toward a more stable midpoint supports a balanced design. Proposing <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a cautious, robustness-preserving step.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "a79c0cc0-62f8-4c97-9c6e-39c686865413"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the move toward stability at x=2, but I believe we can find a safer middle ground that better balances everyone's concerns. <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "a79c0cc0-62f8-4c97-9c6e-39c686865413"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "a79c0cc0-62f8-4c97-9c6e-39c686865413"}, {"answer": "\nThe group is circling between 1 and 2, but we haven't fully explored the upper range. Let me propose <VALUE>4</VALUE> to test whether a bolder positive commitment could work for everyone.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "a79c0cc0-62f8-4c97-9c6e-39c686865413"}, {"answer": "\nFrom 4, a cautious step down improves balance and tests robustness without overcommitting.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "a79c0cc0-6