lder B's attempt at balance, but I believe we're moving too quickly away from the cautious consensus that was forming around -2. Let's return to that stable anchor point: <VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "3657b764-23c7-40c2-915f-4bd5d36bf6b8"}, {"answer": "\nWe seem to be oscillating between -1 and -2 without genuine exploration. Let me advocate again for testing a slightly bolder position that was previously on the table: <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "3657b764-23c7-40c2-915f-4bd5d36bf6b8"}, {"answer": "\nReturning to the midpoint that already drew multiple nods keeps us aligned and stable: <VALUE>-2</VALUE>.\nIf this holds, we can cautiously test a small step higher next to gauge comfort.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "3657b764-23c7-40c2-915f-4bd5d36bf6b8"}, {"answer": "\nTo maintain stability while testing a cautious improvement, let\u2019s move one notch up from the current anchor.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nThis keeps us close to consensus and should be robust enough for evaluation.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "3657b764-23c7-40c2-915f-4bd5d36bf6b8"}, {"answer": "\nWe continue to cycle between the same two positions without resolution. Let's anchor at the point that drew the strongest multi-party support: <VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "3657b764-23c7-40c2-915f-4bd5d36bf6b8"}, {"answer": "To break the loop while preserving stability, let\u2019s take a single step upward and reassess. <VALUE>-1</VALUE> This stays close to the anchor and should reveal whether modest positive movement remains robust.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "3657b764-23c7-40c2-915f-4bd5d36bf6b8"}, {"answer": "\n-1\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "3657b764-23c7-40c2-915f-4bd5d36bf6b8"}, {"answer": "\nWe've exhausted the -1 to -2 corridor without